course: dictionary
lesson: 13334
title: Words in the news
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A news story uses special words to tell you what happened. When you meet a new word, look at the words around it, because they are its context and they give clues. «A lone gunman was seen running from the bank.» The word lone means only one, and running from the bank tells you something bad happened there.
explain: Gunman is a noun. It is the name for the person who attacks people with a gun or uses a gun to commit a crime. «The gunman was arrested by the police» tells you the person who did the crime was caught.
explain: News stories are written to tell facts, not to scare you. If a story about danger frightens you, that is normal. Tell an adult you trust, and remember that adults and the police are there to keep you safe.
fact: A gunman is a man who uses a gun to hurt people or commit a crime.
fact: «A lone gunman» means one person acting alone.
fact: «The gunman was arrested» means the police caught the person.
fact: If you ever feel unsafe, run away, hide, and tell a trusted adult or the police.
fact: A dictionary helps you check the meaning of a word when the context is not enough.
exercise: «The gunman was arrested by the police.» What is a gunman? | A sports player who scores goals | *A person who uses a gun to hurt people or commit a crime | A shopkeeper who sells guns | A police officer who keeps the town safe
exercise: In a news story, «a lone gunman» means | *One person acting alone | A famous singer | A group of friendly guards | A kind old man who gives sweets
exercise: In a safety lesson, you hear a loud danger nearby. What should you do first? | *Run, hide, and tell a trusted adult or the police | Stay still and film it on your phone | Shout at the danger to make it stop | Go outside and look for the danger
test: Which word means a person who uses a gun to hurt people or commit a crime? | *Gunman | Referee | Robber | Soldier
test: Which sentence shows the gunman was caught? | The gunman was sitting in the park. | The gunman was a friendly man. | The gunman was born in May. | *The gunman was arrested.
exam: Why do safety lessons teach children to run, hide and tell an adult if there is danger? | *To keep themselves safe and get help from adults | To play a game with the danger | To make the danger bigger | To find the gunman and catch him
